# local-capable-remote-models.psv — policy for the remote roster local-capable filter.
#
# This file is DATA (no executable code). It declares which remote roster entries are
# reasonably runnable locally on this 128 GB unified-memory stack, so the remote picker
# can hide them by default and the user can review / unhide them interactively.
#
# Format — one entry per line, seven '|'-separated fields:
#
#   provider|remote_model_id|classification|local_artifact|runtime|estimated_size_gb|reason
#
#   provider           must match the provider field in config/remote-agents.sh exactly
#   remote_model_id    must match the model-id field in config/remote-agents.sh exactly
#   classification     one of: local-capable | remote-preferred | unknown
#   local_artifact     path / repo hint for the on-disk or downloadable equivalent (may be empty)
#   runtime            backend that would serve the local equivalent (mlx-lm / rapid / vllm / ...)
#   estimated_size_gb  rough artifact size, for planning
#   reason             short evidence citation — what makes this local-capable (or not)
#
# Rules:
#   - comments (#) and blank lines are ignored
#   - exact (provider, remote_model_id) keys — no fuzzy matching
#   - duplicate keys are rejected by the parser
#   - unknown / missing entries remain visible (fail-open)
#   - parameter count alone is NOT a decision factor; artifact size, backend support,
#     and context/KV overhead matter more
#
# Classification guide:
#   local-capable    — a viable local artifact exists or has a documented conversion route,
#                      the runtime is supported locally, and the artifact + KV overhead fits
#                      on the 128 GB unified-memory machine within the configured memory floor.
#                      Hidden by default in the remote picker.
#   remote-preferred — no defensible local path; remote is the right lane.
#                      Visible in the remote picker.
#   unknown          — insufficient evidence to classify; remain visible until research lands.

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NVIDIA NIM — most of these have MLX-compatible artifacts in the local catalog or are
# large enough that running them locally would consume most of the 128 GB RAM.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Nemotron 3 Super 120B-A3B — large MoE; even at 4-bit plus KV overhead it consumes
# most of the 128 GB RAM. Remote is the right lane.
nvidia|nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b|potentially-local-capable||nvidia-nim|60.0|auto-estimated 68 GB at 4bit: ~68 GB against a 96 GB budget (28 GB spare) — over half the budget, where KV growth and quantization choices the model id cannot reveal could decide it, so it needs real evidence before being hidden (stays visible) [prior note, size math does not refute it: Too large for local; ~80+ GB at 4-bit including KV overhead]

# Nemotron 3 Ultra 550B-A55B — far too large for local (4-bit still ~80+ GB including KV).
nvidia|nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b|remote-preferred||nvidia-nim||Too large for local; ~80+ GB at 4-bit including KV overhead

# Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B — MoE, small, local artifact exists
nvidia|nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b|local-capable|mlx-community/Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-4bit|mlx-lm|6|Small MoE; MLX artifact in catalog; best utility pick locally

# Kimi K3 — Moonshot model, no MLX artifact; remote-only
nvidia|moonshotai/kimi-k3|remote-preferred||nvidia-nim||No MLX artifact; remote-only route

# DeepSeek V4 Flash — no MLX artifact; remote-only
nvidia|deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash-0731|remote-preferred||nvidia-nim||No MLX artifact; remote-only route

# Laguna XS 2.1 (Poolside) — no MLX artifact
nvidia|poolside/laguna-xs-2.1|remote-preferred||nvidia-nim||No MLX artifact; remote-only route

# gpt-oss-20b — OpenAI model via NIM; no local equivalent
nvidia|openai/gpt-oss-20b|local-capable||nvidia-nim|10.0|auto-estimated 18 GB at 4bit: ~18 GB (weights 10 + 8 overhead) fits the 96 GB budget with room to spare — comfortably local, no further math needed [prior note, size math does not refute it: No local equivalent; OpenAI-native model]

# GLM 5.3 Flash — Z.AI model via NIM; no MLX artifact
nvidia|z-ai/glm-5.3-flash|remote-preferred||nvidia-nim||No MLX artifact; remote-only route

# Muse Glimmer 30B (Meta) — MLX artifact exists in local catalog
nvidia|meta/muse-glimmer-30b|local-capable|mlx-community/Muse-Glimmer-30B-4bit|mlx-lm|18|MLX 4-bit artifact in local catalog

# Gemma 4 31B — MLX artifact exists in catalog
nvidia|google/gemma-4-31b-it|local-capable|mlx-community/gemma-4-31b-it-4bit|mlx-lm|18|MLX 4-bit artifact in local catalog

# Kimi K2.6 — no MLX artifact
nvidia|moonshotai/kimi-k2.6|remote-preferred||nvidia-nim||No MLX artifact; remote-only route

# Nemotron Nano 3 30B-A3B — small, but no MLX artifact confirmed
nvidia|nvidia/nemotron-nano-3-30b-a3b|local-capable||nvidia-nim|15.0|auto-estimated 23 GB at 4bit: ~23 GB (weights 15 + 8 overhead) fits the 96 GB budget with room to spare — comfortably local, no further math needed [prior note, size math does not refute it: No confirmed MLX artifact; retest before local use]

# Nemotron 4 340B — far too large
nvidia|nvidia/nemotron-4-340b|remote-preferred||nvidia-nim||Too large for local; ~50+ GB even at 4-bit

# Minitron 12B — small, but no MLX artifact confirmed
nvidia|nvidia/minitron-12b|local-capable||nvidia-nim|6.0|auto-estimated 14 GB at 4bit: ~14 GB (weights 6 + 8 overhead) fits the 96 GB budget with room to spare — comfortably local, no further math needed [prior note, size math does not refute it: No confirmed MLX artifact; retest before local use]

